# Docker
#
# `.dockerignore` used to be listed here and no longer is (C17). A build
# context exclusion file is CONFIGURATION, on the same footing as the Dockerfile
# beside it: ignoring it means every build runs with whatever exclusions the
# machine happens to have, which is how the bundled image ended up shipping a
# 1.18 GB context nobody noticed. Two are tracked now — one at the repository
# root and one in `ai-service/`, because a `.dockerignore` only governs the
# context it sits at the root of.
docker-compose.override.yml
*.dockerfile.local

